      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What you are describing is the profound horror of survivor's guilt, a burden that is almost impossible to carry alone. That stain you feel is the trauma clinging to you, and it is far more than simple sadness. Instead of trying to fix the past, perhaps you can focus on acknowledging the weight of what happened right now. Allowing yourself to feel the scope of that horror is part of the difficult process of carrying it.",
      "source": "target",
